From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ar <sm64ar@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Draw roles and light view

ROLE tags tell the renderer what a draw is, so it can light it and decide
what casts and receives shadows: terrain, object, shadow, effect, water and
lava. The game emits them with gArMode; gfx_pc reports them through the hook
table, together with each WORLD triangle's material flags (lit, texgen).

- weather and particle lists (snow, underwater specks, flowers, lava
  bubbles) are EFFECT: lit, but neither cast nor occlude, so their changing
  count does not alter the static scene;
- water boxes and the water/lava movtex quads are WATER and LAVA; Bowser in
  the Fire Sea's arena draws its lava sea inside a static list, so terrain
  draws that load that texture are LAVA too. The texture state starts afresh
  every frame;
- the host can set a light view, the rotation used for lights (not texgen)
  of WORLD draws, overriding the lighting camera.

Tags and lighting only: what the game draws and does is unchanged.
